# VHS tape for the "Working with agents" demo: print a brief, pipe it into
# `claude -p`, and confirm the result. The Claude turn is real, so it needs a
# logged-in `claude` CLI and makes one API call per recording; its reply and
# timing vary between takes. Recorded by scripts/demo/record.sh, which also
# clamps the wait for the model; see scripts/demo/README.md.

Output docs/assets/img/demo-agent.gif

Set Shell bash
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"
Set FontSize 14
Set Width 1000
Set Height 840
Set Padding 20
Set WindowBar Colorful
Set BorderRadius 8
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Set Framerate 24
Set CursorBlink false

# Keep the real HOME so `claude` finds its login; the demo database is wired
# through XDG_CONFIG_HOME instead. Run from the sandbox so Claude's working
# directory holds nothing but its permission settings.
Hide
Type `THINGS_DEMO_KEEP_HOME=1 source scripts/demo/env.sh && cd "$DEMO_HOME" && clear` Enter
Sleep 1.5s
Show

Sleep 800ms
Type `things show "release candidate" --agent` Enter
Sleep 3s

Type `things show "release candidate" --agent | claude -p "mark it done" --allowedTools "Bash(things:*)"` Enter
# Generous: record.sh clamps the idle stretch to 3s afterwards.
Sleep 60s

Type "things search release" Enter
Sleep 4s
